 # Changelog
 
+## Unreleased
+
+### Sports
+
+- **MMA and Formula 1 join the Sports tab as fixture feeds.** MMA reads API-Sports' `/fights` (two fighters on a card, in a weight class, with the finish method instead of a score) and Formula 1 reads `/races` by season, filtered to the day (a Grand Prix at its circuit, with the session instead of a score). Both are their own API-Sports products on their own hosts, so they need their own keys - `mma:...` / `formula-1:...` in `apiSportsKeys`, or a bare key from a plan that covers them - and MMA joins the default-enabled sports. With no key for them the board stays guide-only for those sports, as it already was.
+- **MotoGP, NASCAR, IndyCar, WEC, WRC and Formula E join as guide-only sports.** API-Sports sells no product for any of them, so there is no feed to give them a host - their events come off the guide like golf and boxing already do, with their own chips, icons and keywords (`ufc`, `mma`, `bellator`, `pfl`, `one championship`, `motogp`, `nascar`, `indycar`, `wec`, `wrc`, `formula e`). MotoGP no longer files under the Formula 1 chip, including "MotoGP Qualifying", which used to lose to Formula 1's own "qualifying" keyword.
+- **Event rows hide the score boxes.** A fight or a race has no score to show, so the row shows the two names and the card or series line instead of a pair of "–" boxes.
+- **An MMA event offers the fight chat.** Tapping a fight shows Watch or Fight chat: the chat opens the built-in IRC client on the Modding Cartel fight channel, titled with the fight, so the chat belongs to that card.
+
+### Fight chat (Modding Cartel IRC)
+
+- **Built-in IRC client, no app-switching.** Connects to irc.obnoxious.lol:6697 over TLS (trusted certificates only, no bypass, no server password), one channel, nickname configurable in the chat view itself (default `nuroctane`). Connect, join, read PRIVMSG, send, PING/PONG, reconnect on drop with backoff, JOIN/PART notices.
+- **Two ways in.** Standalone from the MMA section (an event's Fight chat row, titled with the fight) and as a toggleable panel over playback from the player options (More → Fight chat), where the video keeps playing underneath; Back closes the panel first.
+- **Channel is configurable, default blank on purpose.** The fight site never publishes the channel name in any page or bundle it serves, so there is no honest value to ship: the first open asks for it once and remembers it.
+- **UI patterns adapted from IRCCloud for Android (Apache-2.0):** RecyclerView message list, one deterministic colour per nick, timestamps, auto-scroll that only follows while already at the bottom. Revolution IRC (GPL-3.0) was studied for the same UX behaviour only; none of its code is copied, since GPL-3.0 cannot be combined into this PolyForm Noncommercial codebase.
+
+### Player
+
+- **A live HLS stream that falls behind its playlist window re-anchors to the live edge instead of erroring.** Behind-live-window used to run the generic failover, which replayed the same URL from position 0 - itself behind the window - and errored again. The player now seeks to the default position and prepares, the recovery the Media3 demo app uses for the same error. HLS, adaptive quality, fast start, seek, subtitles, external-player handoff and debrid/torrent handling are otherwise unchanged: they were already covered (DefaultMediaSourceFactory, Auto video + track picker, fast-zap LoadControl, TorrentEngine's local HTTP server, ExternalPlayer).
+
+### Patched build
+
+- **This patch set ships as versionCode 71001 (versionName stays 7.1), release-signed with a locally generated key, and debuggable.** Debuggable is deliberate: it is what lets the app's private data be provisioned on the TV with `adb shell run-as` (plugins, addons, prefs) instead of hand-driving the UI. Single-user TV build, never shipped to a store.
+
